    "description": "MACY’S TECHNOLOGY, JOHNS CREEK, GA\t1999 – PRESENT\nTechnology division of Omnichannel Retailer Macy’s Inc.\n\nSenior Software Engineer, Inventory Systems - Enterprise Receiving, RFID, Inventory Reconciliation & Merchandise Movement System\t2016 – Present\n\nAnalyzed and determined necessary application modifications to ensure product applications met the growing needs of the company. Technically led team of software engineers to deliver software solutions that aligned with the enterprise initiatives. Collaborated with various internal teams as the SME.  \n\no\tDesign architect applications that are optimized for scalability, availability and performance to meet the growing enterprise needs.  \no\tLead software engineering team through the SDLC (Software Development Life Cycle) process which includes design, development, testing and deployment of software solutions using Git.\no\tEffectively communicate with business partners, end users, executive management and software engineering team about project scope and timeline and technical approach.\no\tCollaborate with software engineering teams to ensure use of defined enterprise architecture and coding standards; perform architecture and code reviews with software engineering teams.\no\tDesign and implement an inventory package tracking application using NCR Teradata, Microsoft SSIS and SSRS technologies. \no\tDocument test verification supporting SOX compliance using Bug tracker, SQL Assistant, Excel and Word within a Q4M framework.\no\tLead the development estimates and sizings for the product systems based on business requirements.\no\tDesign, develop, and implement a solution to improve the performance of Teradata SQLs and table rekeying, restructure existing code path to handle multithreading and load balancing issues \no\tCollaborate with various teams on enterprise wide projects.",
